The Bernoulli measure is a probability measure which samples `bool` and--for some $p \in [0, 1]$--samples `true` with proportion $p$ and `false` with proportion $1-p$.
This is done by scaling the `f64` interval $[0, 1]$ to the discrete `u64` interval $[0, 2^{64} - 1]$ and leveraging `Rng::next_u64` for our randomness.

